                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    jcr:title="Building on expertise to tackle difficult-to-treat cancers"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                    type="h3"
                                    variant="h"/>
                                <text2_1220760296
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2025-06-06T02:02:15.119-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="singarx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    text="&lt;p>With over 200 different types of cancers and 50% of people in the UK set to develop cancer within their lifetime, cancer represents a complex and unrelenting healthcare challenge.&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;At AbbVie, we are committed to transforming standards of care across multiple cancers, advancing a dynamic pipeline of investigational therapies, and accelerating the future of oncology. &lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                                <separator
                                    cq:styleIds="[1662756456518]"
                                    jcr:created="{Date}2023-08-09T13:53:37.870-04:00"
                                    jcr:createdBy="chiucx"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2023-08-09T13:53:37.870-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="chiucx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/separator/v2/separator"/>
                                <title2
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1651545824678]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2023-08-09T14:05:09.337-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="chiucx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    jcr:title="Research interests"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                    type="h4"
                                    variant="h"/>
                                <text2
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2026-01-15T09:57:31.479-05:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="singarx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    text="&lt;p>New scientific developments hold the potential to make a remarkable impact on difficult-to-treat cancers. We are investing in innovative treatments aiming to ensure greater precision with transformative outcomes for patients.&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;We strive to deliver transformative therapies that uniquely combine our deep and evolving knowledge in core areas of biology with our experience in cutting-edge technologies. &lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Our four core areas of biology; regulated cell death - apoptosis, B-cell signaling, immuno-oncology and Novel tumour targeting, evaluating the science of cancer growth and progression. &lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;li>Our four core technologies; antibody drug conjugates, targeted protein degradation, antibodies, and cellular therapies, are being applied to discover potentially cutting-edge cancer therapies.&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/li>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/ul>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Across the globe, AbbVie scientists and researchers are currently evaluating&amp;nbsp; investigational medicines across solid tumours and blood cancers, with UK trial sites making a key contribution to our oncology research. &lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                            </container4_copy>
                        </par_12>
